{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1445361-poor-orphans","id":1445361,"title":"'Poor' Orphans?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-04-22T16:10:56-07:00","id":1445361,"title":"'Poor' Orphans?","content":"Ok I've been looking at some stuff. I know, I know, I'm late to the party. but I just like Mage. So I found a few things. Like the Orphan's survival guide book. <br /> <br /> A question. The beginner's stuff is around things like 'how to survive in the streets' and 'how to avoid getting robbed horribly'. But here's the thing: <br /> <br /> One of the orphans in question has Matter 2. Another has Correspondence 3. Matter 2 is basic transmutation, with the capability to turn water into wine, or lead into gold. Or you know, milk into cream, etc... Matter 2 can probably let you make the best teas and soups in the world. Correspondence 3 can let you teleport. Life 2 lets you probably be the bestest herbalist and florist ever. Entropy gives luck. <br /> <br /> The question here is... If they ever truly decided, <i>ever truly wanted</i> to do so, would there be any Mage in the world which can't put a roof ove his/ her head? Or at least, some place out of the cold?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T16:26:46-07:00","id":1445372,"title":"","content":"Ah, yes. The 1e supplement, from way back in the day when it was assumed that Orphans had no clue what they were doing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 04-22-2021, 07:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T19:00:27-07:00","id":1445392,"title":"","content":"Haven't done a ton of reading on Orphans, but my understanding is that the disadvantages they face are more social than mechanical. Members of Traditions are more likely to have access to mentorships and communal resources that can support their magical education, whereas a new Orphan Mage doesn't have access to a Library bigger than what a friend will loan them. It's like being a Caitiff in VtM, but less rabid hatred from people who consider you a harbinger of doom, and more patronizing condescension from people who consider you a rube.<br /> <br /> PS But more importantly, you don't have a big club that might defend you against outside threats, even if it's just to reinforce the semblance of united-we-stand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T19:18:20-07:00","id":1445397,"title":"","content":"And even in that 1e book, one of the examples was quite rich.<br /> <br /> But, yeah. I don't like that book because it's spending a lot describing the life of a street mage...when even by the standards of the book Orphans don't need to be poor. An Orphan book should talk about Orphans, &quot;life in the streets&quot; it's an interesting topic but shouldn't be the main focus of the book - and it is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The question here is... If they ever truly decided, <i>ever truly wanted</i> to do so, would there be any Mage in the world which can't put a roof ove his/ her head? Or at least, some place out of the cold?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think most mages that live in true poverty do so because they don't value material wealth for some reason, or they don't like or see themselves using magick to get easy money for some reason<br /> <br /> Some Paradigms may have a harder time making money with certain Spheres than others, but a decided Mage shouldn't find too hard to get at least a low middle class lifestyle, no matter how unfortunate the Focus - I can't imagine a Focus so limited you couldn't monetize it, unless it's a Focus that <i>uses </i>poverty as Instrument, and/or forbbides to use magick to get money<br /> <br /> High Arcane can make holding property a bit challenging, but, again, a decided mage should be able to overcome this (and an unscrupulous one can just steal with impunity)<br /> <br /> It's also a possible consequence of supernatural jinx. Like, being really disliked by the Syndicate, or being cursed by the spirit courts of money.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T23:34:21-07:00","id":1445436,"title":"","content":"Orphans Survival Guide is late 2nd ed (from 1998; also the last book Phil Brucato fully developed).<br /> <br /> The first chapter is alledgedly based on Justin Achilli's own personal experiences with being homeless and are there because not every Mage, let alone Orphan, has learned Matter, and the nature of the Ascension War means that every Awakened is a potential target for Technocracy indoctrination/reeducation or Nephandi corruption (or death from both, as well as witchhunters). Any family, friends, or coworkers are potential targets to be used against you. Even members of the Traditions, who have access to support of a wider group, will often completely abandon their old lives to adapt new identies (shadow names) and/or live off the grid of modern society. Even the book's Wall Street Wizard template,with Resources 5, works to be socially and professionally invisible for her own protection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T06:23:24-07:00","id":1445472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1445361-poor-orphans?p=1445436#post1445436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Orphans Survival Guide is late 2nd ed (from 1998; also the last book Phil Brucato fully developed).</div> </div> </div> </div>Good catch<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and are there because not every Mage, let alone Orphan, has learned Matter </div> </div> </div>Matter =/= the only way to get money with magick. OP premise was that all mages should be able to put a roof over their heads, if they want to<br /> <br /> Mind 1-3 to learn a craft, and learn how to sell your work for enough money to get by (it doesn't need to be an &quot;on the grid&quot; type of work - could be just being good at crafting stuff).<br /> Or use Life to be a herbalist, as OP said.<br /> Or Time 2 to buy small shares in the market or other comodities that are going to increase in price (somehow the Wall Street Wizard manages invisible Resources 5 because she &quot;works to be invisible&quot;...but what I'm suggesting it's WAY more low key than that, Resources 2 just to get off the streets, should be quite easy to hide)<br /> Or Entropy, to win the lotery or in a low key casino (plenty of canon examples), or - if the Technocracy it's everywhere - just to find good stuff to trade as with Time 2.<br /> <br /> Correspondence &amp; Forces 1-3 could be great for a member of the underworld - to hack into computers and other machines, and/or to be very good at stealing and scamming. More honest jobs can benefit to some extent too (electricist?) But I can see that, w/o the rigth abilities, it could be hard to make money out of them.<br /> Prime by itself isn't going to be very useful to gain money, but could be if combined with other Spheres.<br /> Spirit could be, or not, depending on the spirits that you talk to.<br /> <br /> I guess your own Spheres, backgrounds and abilities could be so unfortunate that you can't earn a modest living even with magick w/o making ripples that would send the Technocracy to your door. But I see that posibility as far from certain.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and the nature of the Ascension War means that every Awakened is a potential target for Technocracy indoctrination/reeducation or Nephandi corruption (or death from both, as well as witchhunters). Any family, friends, or coworkers are potential targets to be used against you.Even members of the Traditions, who have access to support of a wider group, will often completely abandon their old lives to adapt new identies (shadow names) and/or live off the grid of modern society.Even the book's Wall Street Wizard template,with Resources 5, works to be socially and professionally invisible for her own protection </div> </div> </div>SO: the Technocracy, Nephandi, etc...are everywhere and you can't do shit w/o becoming a target. OK. Orphans are poor because they're hidding...<br /> <br /> But being poor and off the grid isn't the same thing. Being homeless isn't the only way to be invisible, even as per Orphan's Survival Guide.<br /> <br /> Maybe you want to make an Orphan, but don't care so much about being poor. Don't make an Orphan, then? - not even this book says such a thing, as you have the option to be rich if you &quot;work to be socially and professionally invisible&quot;, as you say.<br /> <br /> Yet <b>that </b>(to be socially and professionally invisible, as to avoid the Technocracy) is something the book literally never talks about outside one <i>character sheet...</i>Or am I wrong?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-23-2021, 11:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T07:18:11-07:00","id":1445480,"title":"","content":"Yeah, my bad. I was thinking of Outcasts. <br /> <br /> As well, Brucato seems to have changed his mind. As of M20, Orphans bear little resemblance to the stuff described in the Orphan's Survival Guide. They're pretty much just like any other mage, except that they don't have membership in an exclusive club. Financially, they can be anywhere from destitute to multi-billionaire. They can have remarkably consistent and robust systems of magic. It's almost as if you don't need some centuries old conspiracy telling you what to think.<br /> <br /> A case could be made that Orphan's Survival Guide, and everything that came before it, is Traditionist propaganda. Certainly, \u201cOrphan\u201d is a slur; and the idea that life outside of the Traditions amounts to scraping by on the streets is exactly the sort of thing that strokes a Traditionist ego.<br /> <br /> <i>Are</i> there independent mages who fit the Orphan stereotype? Sure! No stereotype exists without some basis in fact. But they're not nearly as common as they would like you to believe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 04-23-2021, 09:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T12:49:24-07:00","id":1445521,"title":"","content":"In a lot of ways, OSG is something of an update of WoD: Outcasts Hollow Ones section and Destiny's Price. Over all, it's a good book. I'm just not sure it's a good <i>Orphans </i>book. The premade character templates are all pretty good Orphan examples though. (However, I'm still disappointed Rogue Technocrat isn't one of them.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T16:24:20-07:00","id":1445566,"title":"","content":"That's another thing I like about the new take on Independent Mages: they let you play an agent, cyborg, gadgeteer, technician, tycoon, etc. without having to be related to the Technocracy at all. Or any other faction, for that matter. Your agent could literally be a CIA agent, for example. Your cyborg could be the product of the OSI (\u201cWe can rebuild him. We have the technology. We can make him better than he was. Better, stronger, faster.\u201d) Your gadgeteer could be a freelancer. Your technician could be on the run from the army. Your tycoon could (and probably does) run his <i>own</i> organization. Yes, any of these could be recast in terms of the Technocracy; but they don't <i>have</i> to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 04-23-2021, 09:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T18:23:31-07:00","id":1445581,"title":"","content":"The status as &quot;poor&quot; orphan could also be seen as a transitory stage, one which many orphans pass through at some point. Not an automatic thing, or a required rite of passage, but something unsurprisingly common.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T20:07:32-07:00","id":1445593,"title":"","content":"An M20 version of a book on Orphans and Initiates (the overlap because it would be geared toward the newly Awakened, but also continue to track those who never are taken in by a mento into a sect) is on my wishlist/possible Vault to do list","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T21:11:49-07:00","id":1445599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1445361-poor-orphans?p=1445566#post1445566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's another thing I like about the new take on Independent Mages: they let you play an agent, cyborg, gadgeteer, technician, tycoon, etc. without having to be related to the Technocracy at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've found it fairly easy to do that with the Traditions as well. But I also had fun adapting Division Six from Hunter: The Vigil into an Orphan faction (a very loose definition of faction here) centered around Washington DC and mostly made up of low and midlevel government workers being subtly guided by someone who may or may not be John Courage. Also, Do-It-Yourself Transhumanist Cyborg makes for a fun Orphan concept, as do things like Gadget-Addicted Cyber-Prep, Bio-Chemist Prodigy who uses custom made designer drugs, Burned Government Agent, and UFO Hunter. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}